WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:02.800
What do you remember about the fans?

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.120
Loud [laughs].

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:14.320
I think here at Tiger Stadium in those days—which I’m quite sure those times will come back—the LSU fans were probably the greatest in the nation.

4
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.380
I think in my last year, after a new addition onto the stadium,

5
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.600
capacity was seventy-eight thousand and . . . There’s just no place like that,

6
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.680
like Tiger Stadium on a Saturday night when it’s full, and the fans are really into the game.

7
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.440
I remember even when I went into the NFL,

8
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:37.180
I’d get a lot of guys asking me about LSU and how was it to play here in Tiger Stadium.

9
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:42.260
And, you know, I would just tell them, “There’s nothing like it.”

10
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:48.860
I really had a difficult time my first couple of years in Cincinnati [with the Bengals] because of that fact.

11
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:57.560
I was used to the crowd getting into the game and being real emotional and with the field being that close to . . . With the stands being that close to the field in Tiger Stadium,

12
00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.020
it was just a different atmosphere.
